Hi Anjali,

Attached are the report from this morning's review and the separate monthly f=
igures. Fare Payments availability for October to December was 99.94%, calcul=
ated over the whole quarter from 4,800 unavailable seconds in 7,948,800 eligi=
ble seconds. The service target remains 99.9% monthly; the quarterly figure i=
s a summary over elapsed time.

Matthew confirmed the two distinct Faregate windows: 42 minutes in November a=
nd 22 minutes 48 seconds in December. Together they account for 3,888 seconds=
, or 81% of the 4,800 seconds lost in the quarter. The remaining interruption=
s account for 912 seconds.

As agreed, Matthew will first rehearse a return to the previous checkout rout=
e and bring the elapsed time and observed outcome by 24 January. I will then =
check that the post-change watch catches a failed checkout completion, with t=
he watched outcome and reviewer acknowledgement, by 31 January. We'll conside=
r broader work on the other interruptions after those results. Both actions a=
re open in the report.

Thanks,
Daniel


